<!--
  Every case 9 §9.1 turns on, in one invented statement.

  The strict rule lets exactly two of these through: the 9.99 monthly
  subscription and the 4.99 one. What it must keep out is the supermarket whose
  visits are regular and whose totals are not, the fuel bought at the same round
  amount on no rhythm, the energy bill that is one cent apart three months
  running, the water mandate that collects whenever the meter is read, and the
  one-off purchases that happen to share a counterparty with a subscription.

  Nine months, opened and closed by the bank's own arithmetic, so the account
  also has a balance AYQ is entitled to state.

  The IBAN is a test number. The creditors do not exist, the mandates are
  invented, and no real statement is anywhere near this file.
-->
